                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Reading: reading_1: Interpret simple charts and graphs related to texts.<br>reading_2: Write responses to questions about informational texts.<br>phonemic_awareness: Demonstrate knowledge of phonemic awareness by segmenting multisyllabic words into syllables.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Reading: Can interpret data about weather patterns in charts (e.g., 'More people like sunny days.').<br>Can answer questions about weather-related texts (e.g., 'What's the weather like tomorrow?' 'It will rain tomorrow.').<br>Can segment multisyllabic words into syllables, demonstrating knowledge of phonemic awareness (e.g., 'thermostat' into 'ther-mo-stat').</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
